# REQUIRES: verilator
# Constant-shell fold, `--link-rings K`: a link memory whose entries are each
# live for a short window of the frame (from the write a read takes to that
# read) keeps K entries (a power of two, at most the option's), the entry's
# index mod K, where the schedule shows no other entry of that address
# written in any read's window; its storage is the schedule's spacing, not
# the instances'. An entry whose window holds K writes or more (the frame's
# wrap) is held at an address of its own past the ring, by table.
# Driver/Inputs/ringlinks: eight groups of eight nodes; a zero-latency chain
# (zout -> zin, late) through the ready-cone class Node_rc, a registered ring
# (rout -> rin, an early chain link) and the groups' pass-through outputs.
# - k8: rings, with shared write registers, takes in the slot and bubbles;
# - h2: two entries held (FOLDSIM_RING_HOLD, a test hook holding the lowest
#   entries read, as a wrap would): a ring of 8 and 2 held, 10 entries;
# - off: no ring without the option.
# Each exact against its target, channels stalled or not.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/ringlinks
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/k8 --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --bubbles --csf-ready-copies Node:2 --csf-ready-cones --link-rings 8 Node Grp 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=K8
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=K8SIM < %t/k8/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/k8/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/k8/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/k8/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/k8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=0 +bubble=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/k8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=40 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_RING_HOLD=2 foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/h2 --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --bubbles --csf-ready-copies Node:2 --csf-ready-cones --link-rings 8 Node Grp 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=H2
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=H2SIM < %t/h2/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/h2/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/h2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/h2/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/h2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 +bubble=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=40 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/off --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --bubbles --csf-ready-copies Node:2 --csf-ready-cones Node Grp 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OFF
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OFFSIM < %t/off/foldsim_sim.mlir
# `--csf-mailbox-hbm-chains`: the early chain link (rout -> rin, each entry
# read by the next node a frame after its write) streams through HBM as a
# reader-indexed mailbox like any other early link (without the option it
# stays an on-chip memory of every node); against the controllers' model
# (Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv: 1 to 80 host cycles, stalls, full, bubbles,
# the protocol checked).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/ch --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 160 --compact-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --bubbles --link-rings 8 --csf-mailbox-hbm --csf-mailbox-hbm-chains Node Grp > %t/ch.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CH < %t/ch/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/ch -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/ch/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/ch/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/ch/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/ch/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/ch/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/ch/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=5 +hi=80 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/nch --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 160 --compact-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --bubbles --link-rings 8 --csf-mailbox-hbm Node Grp > %t/nch.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NCH < %t/nch/schedule.txt
# `--csf-mailbox-hbm-split` (Driver/Inputs/splitpage: four Par of eight Kid; a
# Par register to each child rotated, another to its first child): with rows
# of 8 bits the first child's page (16 bits) passes a row, so the sliced
# stream splits in two (eight pages of 8 bits, one page of 8 bits for the
# first child's second input); without the option the pair is one
# producer-indexed stream of 72-bit words. Exact against the controllers'
# model.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/splitpage
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/sp --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 96 --compact-links --share-links --bubbles --csf-mailbox-hbm --csf-mailbox-hbm-chains --csf-mailbox-hbm-row-bits 8 --csf-mailbox-hbm-split Kid Par > %t/sp.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SP < %t/sp/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/sp -DVM1 -DVM2 -DVM3 -DVM4 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/sp/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/sp/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/sp/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/sp/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/sp/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/sp/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=5 +hi=80 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/nsp --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 96 --compact-links --share-links --bubbles --csf-mailbox-hbm --csf-mailbox-hbm-chains --csf-mailbox-hbm-row-bits 8 Kid Par > %t/nsp.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NSP < %t/nsp/schedule.txt
# SP: link streams: 5 streams, 12 links
# SP: link stream Par_model Kid 8 0 64 8 8 32
# SP-NEXT: link stream Par_model Kid 1 0 8 8 1 4
# NSP: link stream Par_model Kid 9 0 72 72 1 4
# K8: rings 4 (112 bits, 320 as instance memories, 0 held entries)
# H2: rings 1 (80 bits, 224 as instance memories, 2 held entries)
# OFF-NOT: as instance memories
# The late chain's memory: 8 entries (of 28 node instances read), or 10 with
# two held (their addresses by table, registered as the instance is).
# K8SIM: %Node_rc_zout_to_Node_zin_0 = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <8 x 8
# H2SIM-DAG: %Node_rc_zout_to_Node_zin_0_ring0 = seq.firreg
# H2SIM-DAG: %Node_rc_zout_to_Node_zin_0 = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <10 x 8
# OFFSIM: %Node_rc_zout_to_Node_zin_0 = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <28 x 8
# CH: link stream Node Node 1 0 8 8 1 64
# CH: link stream Node Grp_model
# NCH-NOT: link stream Node Node
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
# CHECK-NOT: MISMATCH
